pr_comments:
We need to take a decision on what to do with non-list likes (tuples, None, integer, ellipsis ..). Handle them inside or outside? 

@TomAugspurger preferred to handle them outside, and indeed, that gives the signature of `check_array_indexer` a tighter typing (list-like -> ndarray, otherwise it is Any->Any) 

On the other hand, that makes that basically in all `__getitem__` we need to add a `is_list_like(item) and not isinstance(item, tuple)` before calling `check_array_indexer`. So it was also suggested to have a `check_indexer` with this more relaxed check.
